P-2 (spec 017, the night shift; plan.md §10; research.md R-13; tasks.md T065): CLAUDE.md's Infra and Verifying lines
name the night shift's plan and gate routes.

What it changes: two lines and nothing else.
  - "Infra:": a real plan is a runner request, run as the plan-only role (h4-agent-plan, P-6, in the plan container);
    no make apply; apply stays yours, in your terminal, until publication, then protected CI.
  - "Verifying your work": the conditional "(until they can run, make check)" and "never make check in their own
    terminal" stay; tools/gates/gate <branch> runs in your checkout of main, by you or by a runner (gate) request.
The words saved to fit the cap come from the same two lines: "There is no ... on purpose — apply is a human action",
"and" before make evals, "reporting any task complete, and" became "reporting done;", and "the protected CI
environment" became "protected CI". A pointer to docs/how-we-build/night-shift.md didn't fit. Read them as yours to
reword.

Spec IDs: decision 1 ("Yes, let agents run terraform plan"), decision 2 ("Let agents run tools/gates/gate"), his Q1
answer ("It can use my checkout of main"), FR-015 (plan and gate stay off until CLAUDE.md's and .claude/**'s patches
merge), and the Assumptions' deviation reversing "Before merging, the Author runs tools/gates/gate".

Needed for: plan and gate on (the second install), with P-3 and P-6. Not for the merge itself.

How to apply, on your own branch, from the repository's root (one line each):
  B=feat/017-g5-patches
  F=docs/merge-requests/2026-11-12-feat-017-p2.patch
  git show "refs/heads/$B:$F" > /tmp/p2.patch
  sha256sum /tmp/p2.patch
  patch -p1 --dry-run < /tmp/p2.patch
  patch -p1 < /tmp/p2.patch
The patch touches CLAUDE.md, so the gate's agent-config-evals step waits for make evals-agent-config.

